# =============================================================================
# SCREENING CALIBRATION -- physics identical to molaro_T-20_hcurv_2h_a1e-1_Dv10,
# run on the coarse screening mesh so the two can be differenced.
#
# THIS ARM PRODUCES NO NEW PHYSICS. Its only job is to answer: does the 6.5x
# cheaper mesh reproduce the answer we already paid full price for? Every
# parameter below is copied from the production Dv10 arm -- same wall humidity,
# same D_v, same alpha_c, same CFL setting -- so resolution is the ONLY
# difference between them.
#
# PASS: a = 0.1802 +- 0.0037 over the 44.47-60.43 um width window
#       (the production Dv10 run refitted on this geometry's coverage).
#       Land inside ~10 % of that and the screen is calibrated; sweep away.
# FAIL: a materially off that. Then the coarse mesh is not usable for exponent
#       work and the screening plan needs a finer eps -- learned for ~1 % of
#       the cost of finding out during a sweep.
#
# SECOND JOB: this is the cost-model calibration point. The dom2 -> dom3 jump
# measured ch/step scaling as DoF^2.9, which is NOT safe to extrapolate
# DOWNWARD to a 6.5x smaller mesh. Linear-in-DoF would put this near 2 USD;
# the DoF^2.9 slope would put it near 0.06. Nothing between those is
# predictable without a measurement, so measure it here, on the run whose
# result is useful either way.
#
# T_FINAL 7.0e+03. The production Dv10 arm took 6215 s to cross 44 -> 60.43 um.
# 7.0e3 covers that with ~13 % margin.
#
# Pair with: molaro_2D_L450x225um_eps0.30um_axisym_T-20pair_r22um_screen
# =============================================================================

-t_final 7.0e+03
-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.0000234                     # = 1 + d0*(2/R_avg); grain-matched wall
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-dif_vap 2.178e-04                      # D_v0 x10 -- EFFECTIVE transport

-flag_BC_Tfix 1
-flag_BC_rhovfix 1

-alpha_pointwise 1
-alpha_model 0
-alpha_c0 1.0e-1
-alpha_lo 1.0e-3
-alpha_hi 1.0e-1

-dtmax 2.0e2
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.15                     # matched to the production arm

-t_out_log 80
-t_out_log_t0 2.0e1
